whatsapp-linux-client (1.0.0-2) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Fix dock/app-grid icon showing as generic instead of the app icon on
    GNOME/Wayland: call QApplication.setDesktopFileName() so the compositor
    can match the running window to the installed .desktop entry's Icon=.

 -- Cletus Xavier <cletusxavier3@protonmail.com>  Fri, 28 Aug 2026 01:39:11 +0530

whatsapp-linux-client (1.0.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Rebuild packaging using dh-python/pybuild so the package installs
    correctly to standard Python and desktop-integration paths:
    - whatsapp_linux_client module now installs under the standard
      dist-packages path (previously /usr/lib/whatsapp-linux-client,
      which was never on sys.path).
    - /usr/bin/whatsapp-linux-client launcher is now generated from
      the project's console_scripts entry point (previously missing).
    - .desktop file and icon installation unchanged (already correct).

 -- Cletus Xavier <cletusxavier3@protonmail.com>  Fri, 28 Aug 2026 01:39:11 +0530
